<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nyai Roro Kidul</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ratu Kidul, Kanjeng Ratu Kidul</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nyai Roro Kidul, or Ratu Kidul, is the spirit queen of the Southern Ocean in Javanese belief, associated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>'s south coast. Javanese court tradition holds that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panembahan-senapati">Panembahan Senapati</a>, founder of Mataram, took her as a spiritual consort, and the rulers of Surakarta and Yogyakarta claimed a continuing mystical bond with her. She remains a prominent figure in Javanese folklore and court ritual.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nyai-roro-kidul.jpg" alt="Nyai Roro Kidul" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gunawan Kartapranata · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kanjeng_Ratu_Kidul.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
